  "summary": "Malicious code in tui-react-mobile-styles (npm)",
  "details": "Tui-react-mobile-styles@20.8.7 is a combosquat package that functions as a platform-aware binary dropper. On require(), it fingerprints the host OS and architecture, then downloads a platform-specific binary payload from Cloudflare Workers C2 infrastructure (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS at paths /pkg/package (Linux x64), /pkg/package-arm64 (Linux arm64), /pkg/loader_mac (macOS), or /pkg/package.exe (Windows). If HTTPS fails, it falls back to a DNS TXT-based retrieval channel using c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site for chunked data transfer. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (Linux/macOS) or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe (Windows), made executable, and spawned as a detached background process that outlives the parent.",
  "affected": [
    {
      "package": {
        "ecosystem": "npm",
        "name": "tui-react-mobile-styles",
        "purl": "pkg:npm/tui-react-mobile-styles@20.8.7"
